      "brief": "Hold the four arms of the crossroads until the army arrives, and it arrives one battalion at a time up the Brussels road behind you. You are outnumbered until about the middle of the afternoon and never afterwards, so the ground you give away early is ground you can afford and the crossroads is not. Watch the rye: you have almost no cavalry, his is good, and a battalion caught in column out there has about the time it takes a courier to reach it.",
